-3\\cdot {∇}_{w}(‖w{‖}^{2})-{∇}_{w}(2) \\\\  & =-3\\cdot {∇}_{w}({w}^{T}w)-{∇}_{w}(2) \\\\  & =-3\\cdot 2w+0 \\\\  & =-6w.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544807 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186544652 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544807 #edb/ref 1069 "q-275973" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544807 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544807 #edb/ref 1071 "Given the function \n\n$$\nf(w)=‖w{‖}_{1}-{w}^{T}w\n$$\n\nthat maps a vector to a scalar, find ${∇}_{w}f.$ You may assume that $w$ has all nonzero components." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544807 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3cb041fc-343a-591c-abe2-c70938440309" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544807 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the results\n\n$$\n{∇}_{w}(‖w{‖}_{1})=\\text{sign}(w),\\,{∇}_{w}({w}^{T}w)=2w,\n$$\n\n we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{w}f & ={∇}_{w}(‖w{‖}_{1}-{w}^{T}w) \\\\  & ={∇}_{w}(‖w{‖}_{1})-{∇}_{w}({w}^{T}w) \\\\  & =\\text{sign}(w)-2w.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544835 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186544766 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544835 #edb/ref 1069 "q-275978" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544835 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544835 #edb/ref 1071 "Given the function \n\n$$\nf(x,w)={(‖w{‖}_{1})}^{3}-4{x}^{T}w\n$$\n\nthat maps a vector to a scalar, find ${∇}_{w}f.$ You may assume that $w$ has no zero components." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544835 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7dc41e95-539c-50b9-8fb0-b63764e8684c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544835 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the results\n\n$$\n{∇}_{w}(‖w{‖}_{1})=\\text{sign}(w),\\,{∇}_{w}({x}^{T}w)=x,\n$$\n\n we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{w}f & ={∇}_{w}({(‖w{‖}_{1})}^{3}-4{x}^{T}w) \\\\  & ={∇}_{w}({(‖w{‖}_{1})}^{3})-{∇}_{w}(4{x}^{T}w) \\\\  & ={∇}_{w}({(‖w{‖}_{1})}^{3})-4\\cdot {∇}_{w}({x}^{T}w) \\\\  & =3(‖w{‖}_{1})^{2}\\cdot {∇}_{w}(‖w{‖}_{1})-4\\cdot x \\\\  & =3(‖w{‖}_{1})^{2}\\cdot \\text{sign}(w)-4\\cdot x \\\\  & =3(‖w{‖}_{1})^{2}\\cdot \\text{sign}(w)-4x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544884 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186544697 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544884 #edb/ref 1069 "q-265746" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544884 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544884 #edb/ref 1071 "Given the function \n\n$$\nf(x,w)=3{w}^{T}x-‖w{‖}^{2}+1\n$$\n\nthat maps two vectors to a scalar, find ${∇}_{w}f.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544884 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d8c2cd33-feb8-5850-af19-6e3631c29b25" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544884 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the results \n\n$$\n{∇}_{w}({w}^{T}x)=x,\\,{∇}_{w}({w}^{T}w)=2w,\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{w}f & ={∇}_{w}(3{w}^{T}x-‖w{‖}^{2}+1) \\\\  & =3\\cdot {∇}_{w}({w}^{T}x)-{∇}_{w}(‖w{‖}^{2})+{∇}_{w}(1) \\\\  & =3\\cdot {∇}_{w}({w}^{T}x)-{∇}_{w}({w}^{T}w)+{∇}_{w}(1) \\\\  & =3\\cdot x-2w+0 \\\\  & =3x-2w.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544922 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186544947 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544922 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "45be477a-4758-5690-b800-0acb22740f26" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544922 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186544792 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544947 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186544992 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544947 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7fbe5f30-b984-5b5a-bcf7-21b4ac60ddeb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544947 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186544884 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544969 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c0ed2fb4-d964-5c56-afa4-a060d0c3984c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544969 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186544835 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544973 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186544969 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544973 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c768ad34-e503-5b15-94e2-cfeb4be99419" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544973 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186544807 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544992 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 1759218654497